WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.100
On August 28, 2020, news broke that Chadwick
Boseman unexpectedly died at the age of 43.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.180
The actor, who was famous for playing T'Challa,
the MCU's Black Panther and King of Wakanda,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.560
was easily one of the greatest and most influential
stars of our time.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.880
Boseman passed away after a four-year-long
battle with colon cancer.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.180
In fact, he was fighting the disease throughout
the four years he made his last seven movies.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.340
When Boseman's official Twitter account broke
the tragic news, the world was in shock.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:32.120
The outpouring of love from the actor's fans
and fellow celebrities was immediate and heartfelt.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.300
People paid their respects and fondly remembered
his many great roles, as well as the way his

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.220
role as T'Challa proved that representation
matters.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.940
Apart from the vast human and cultural tragedy
of Boseman's death, it also created a difficult

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.100
problem for Disney and its subsidiary Marvel
Studios.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.440
Black Panther is already a billion-dollar
cinematic entity, and Boseman would arguably

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.020
have been the most beloved and bankable star
of the next few phases of the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:55.860
Universe.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:00.120
With the actor's popularity and the character's
in-universe role as an intelligent superhero

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.080
with access to amazing technology, Boseman's
T'Challa was essentially the current MCU's

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.659
answer to former franchise lynchpin Tony Stark.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.700
So, how is Disney dealing with this difficult
and heartbreaking situation?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.720
Disney representatives say they're not focused
on figuring out what to do with Black Panther

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.820
2, at least, not quite yet.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.700
According to The Hollywood Reporter, sources
within the Disney corporation have stated

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.560
that the company is, quote, "processing the
grief of a loved one," and paying homage to

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.520
Boseman.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.720
As such, they have no immediate plans to shift
focus to the Black Panther sequel, and aren't

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.479
offering up any details about what such a
sequel would even look like, as of the making

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.540
of this video.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.420
Boseman wanted to keep his illness as private
as possible.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.080
As such, only a few people outside his family
knew about his cancer diagnosis and subsequent

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:43.960
battle at all.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.520
The MCU at large, in fact, was so deeply in
the dark about Boseman's situation that the

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.549
news only reached Marvel head honcho Kevin
Feige's inbox on the day the Black Panther

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:53.480
actor died.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.960
As such, the MCU's reaction to Boseman's death
was that of stunned heartbreak, followed by

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.480
touching memories of their beloved co-star
and friend.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.619
Robert Downey Jr. even called Boseman and
his achievements the high point of the entire

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.240
MCU.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:11.180
"Black Panther is hands down, it is the crowning
achievement of the Marvel universe."

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.159
The Iron Man star elaborated to Good Morning
America,

00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:18.060
"It was the one where people got to vote with
their ticket sales and say: 'We require this

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.290
overdue diversity.'"

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.190
At some point Disney and Marvel executives
will have to lift the veil of sorrow and ask

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.020
themselves the difficult question: How should
things go forward without Boseman?

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.260
"I am not ready to be without you."

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.780
Disney has faced this uniquely tragic situation
before, unfortunately.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.140
In 2016, the company had to figure out how
to proceed with The Rise of Skywalker when

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.500
the esteemed Carrie Fisher, who played Princess
Leia, died at 60.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:47.060
In the same vein, Universal had to painstakingly
recreate Paul Walker when the actor passed

00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:50.819
away in a car accident as shooting Fast &amp; Furious
7 was taking place.

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:54.790
However, Boseman was the star of his own,
incredibly successful movie, and he was a

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.090
major player in the notoriously interconnected
MCU in general.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.970
While Disney could cancel Black Panther 2
and quietly write T'Challa out of the MCU,

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.939
seeing as the first movie was a cultural,
critical, and financial success and that Boseman's

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:11.060
death will have to be addressed in some fashion,
some believe that's an unlikely outcome.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.840
Other observers think that the company could
try to replace Boseman with another actor,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.180
but that's bound to cause a massive outcry,
and for good reason.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.379
Knowing this, many think that a better option
might be to take a page from the comic books

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.500
and hand the Black Panther mantle to Shuri,
T'Challa's younger sister, played by Letitia

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.380
Wright.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:31.720
The tenacious and tech-savvy Shuri is a popular
character, and her ascension to full Black

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.280
Panther-hood is already something fans want
to see in Black Panther 2.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.000
This idea has even pushed some fans to start
petitioning for Disney and Marvel to tap Shuri

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.580
to become the next Black Panther.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.300
Regardless of what's going to happen, the
MCU, and the world, has lost a true giant

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.640
in Chadwick Boseman.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.420
As Black Panther director Ryan Coogler put
it:

00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:54.819
"I spent the last year preparing, imagining
and writing words for him to say that we weren't

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:55.920
destined to see.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.560
It leaves me broken knowing that I won't be
able to watch another close-up of him in the

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.620
monitor again or walk up to him and ask for
another take."

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.300
Our thoughts are with Boseman's friends and
family during this time of grief.

